con EPOC, afectando su pronóstico.", "EXACERBACIONES:Las exacerbaciones son episodios agudos de empeoramiento de los síntomas en pacientes con EPOC, que pueden requerir atención médica.", "INGRESOS HOSPITALARIOS:Los ingresos hospitalarios son una medida de la gravedad de la EPOC y su impacto en la salud del paciente.", "CIRROSIS BILIAR FOCAL:Focal biliary cirrhosis is a liver condition that can develop in patients with cystic fibrosis, characterized by damage to the bile ducts.", "ALTERACIONES DEL METABOLISMO HIDROCARBONADO:Alterations in carbohydrate metabolism are common in cystic fibrosis patients, leading to complications such as diabetes.", "DIABETES RELACIONADA CON LA FQ:Diabetes related to cystic fibrosis is a common complication that increases with age among affected individuals.", "ÍLEO MECONIAL:ÍLEO MECONIAL refers to a medical condition known as meconium ileus, which occurs in approximately 5% of patients with cystic fibrosis. This condition is characterized by intestinal obstruction at birth due to the blockage of the intestines by thick meconium. As a result, affected newborns require prompt medical treatment to address the obstruction and manage the associated complications.", "ALFA-1-ANTITRIPSINA:ALFA-1-ANTITRIPSINA, also known as alpha-1-antitrypsin, is a protein that plays a critical role in protecting the lungs. It is particularly relevant in the context of various pulmonary diseases. A deficiency in this protein can lead to serious lung conditions, such as emphysema, and it is commonly tested in patients who present with respiratory symptoms.", "PACIENTE FUMADOR:A smoker patient with respiratory symptoms who may be at risk for developing EPOC and other lung diseases.", "SÍNDROME DE DESNUTRICIÓN:Malnutrition syndrome refers to a range of conditions resulting from inadequate intake of nutrients, which is prevalent in patients with chronic diseases such as cystic fibrosis and EPOC."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0